  //      reaches zero integrates, and the gate's faint always-on tail will
  //      whiten the entire sea over a minute if it is allowed through;
  //   2. THE SEA-STATE COUPLING. breakAmt scales with wind energy (×0.54 at
  //      open, ×1.25 at storm), so a low threshold saturates for both states and
  //      the ocean stops caring about the weather. Cutting high up the
  //      distribution is what turns that ×2.3 in amplitude into an order of
  //      magnitude in COVERAGE: open keeps a few percent of breaking crest, a
  //      storm streaks most of the surface.
  // TWO couplings, deliberately. The smoothstep is a DUTY gate (how often a fixed
  // point deposits at all) and the linear factor is an AMPLITUDE one (how much per
  // event). A saturating gate alone gave r1 no state coupling — open and storm
