  // shut below σ≈0.09), coastal laps, a storm breaks — and dBreak has already
  // moved the line from ~10 m offshore at coastal to ~80 m at storm, so the
  // state changes the surf zone's SIZE as well as its energy.
  // r3 ran this to 2.9 at storm which, times the rate, saturated every texel on
  // the beach to 1.0 within a tenth of a second — and a saturated field has NO
  // STRUCTURE, because min(1.0, …) throws the streak modulation away. The span is
  // now deliberately narrow (×0.48 coastal → ×1.7 storm): the state's real
  // coupling is dBreak moving the break line from ~10 m offshore to ~90 m, not the
  // deposit amplitude.
